# This file (i.e., at `~/…/Dropbox/Users/jim/Prefs/Meta/finder_sidebar_favorites_name_path_pairs.jsonl`)
# is a template to be copied to a particular user’s ``~/…/Dropbox/Users/$USER/Prefs/Meta`
# directory, from which location it would be customized to the particular user’s
# desires.
#
# The ultimate file for a particular user includes an ordered list of JSON ["nickname", "path"]
# pairs of objects (files or directories) to be added to the Finder’s sidebar as Favorites.
#
# Typically:
# - one pair per line
# - no comma at the end of any pair
# - blank lines are OK.
#
# The path can start with '~' or '~/', in which case the '~' will be expanded to be "$HOME".
# The nickname can either be (a) the filename-only part of the path or (b) a different
# string that should appear as the Finder sidebar Favorite. In this case, the nickname
# nevertheless must be a valid filename. 
#
# This template is designed to have a variety of (name, path) pairs that might be useful
# to a particular user, so that the unhelpful lines can be deleted and other lines added.
#
# This file may have (a) leading comment lines (beginning with a '#') and (b) blank lines
# throughout.
#
# A guide to some of the below separators:
#   ⬇️⬇️ -- 🌐 -- ⬇️⬇️				Items directly below are in the network scope, e.g., AirDrop,
#                             connected servers, etc.
#   ⬇️⬇️ -- 🖥️ -- ⬇️⬇️				Items directly below are at the computer level (but above
#                              the user level), e.g., `/Applications`
#   ⬇️⬇️ -- 🏠 -- ⬇️⬇️       Items directly below are at the active-user level
#   ⬇️⬇️--PROTON--⬇️⬇️       Items directly below are in the Proton Drive cloud service.
#   ⬇️⬇️--DROPBOX--⬇️⬇️      Items directly below are in the Dropbox cloud service
#   ⬇️--DB/Users--⬇️         Items directly below are in the 'Users' subdirectory of Dropbox
#   ⬇️--DB/Users/Me--⬇️      Items directly below are in the particular active user’s 
#                             subdirectory of the Dropbox/Users directory. ('Me' could be 
#                             changed to the user’s actual shortname.)
#   ⬇️--DB/Users/🤷🏻--⬇️      Items directly below are in some other user’s subdirectory
#                             of the Dropbox/Users directory.
#   ⬇️--DB/etc--⬇️            Items directly below are (a) in Dropbox but (b) outside
#                             Dropbox/Users
#   --------------------n     Used as miscellaneous visual separators to deploy where
#                             helpful in the Finder’s sidebar Favorites area. (The digit(s)
#                             is/are there to make each separator uniquely named.)

